                <pb facs="0098" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg78"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center"><seg type="margin">[415]</seg> *[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Governor Perdigao to
                        the captain of the port of Funchal</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Civil
                                Government of Funchal</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1864</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir</hi>: I have just been informed,
                    by an official communication from yourself, that the ship Florida, a South
                    American corsair, sailing under the so-called flag of the Confederate States,
                    which have not been recognized by us, has entered and is now at anchor in this
                    port.</p>
                <p>In view of the decree of the 29th July, 1861, a vessel in those circumstances can
                    only enter the ports of Portugal when compelled thereto by <hi
                        rendition="#italic">force majeure;</hi> and as such case has not happened,
                    nor is it invoked by the commander of said vessel to legalize or justify his
                    stay in this port,. I find myself compelled, in conformity to the law, and in
                    obedience to all <pb facs="0099" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/> those principles of
                    loyalty which are due to the flag of a friendly nation, to request that your
                    excellency will be pleased to intimate to the aforesaid commander to leave this
                    port with all possible speed.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will be pleased to keep me informed of all that may occur in
                    carrying out the present commission.</p>
                <p>God preserve your excellency.</p>
                <p>The civil governor,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAOINTHO ANTONIO PERDIGAO.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Captain</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Of the Port of Funchal.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
